## Inline Formatting & Nested Constructs

Writing in Markdown XL allows fluent combination of typographic tags:
Here is normal text containing **strong bold words**, _emphasized italics_, and nested **_bold italic elements_**. 

We can also mark critical terms using the native highlighter ::high-priority feature::, or mark deprecated syntax using the redaction tag ||legacy Win32 GDI call||. Authors can write inline private notes ++verify DirectX 12 D2D fallback++ that are omitted during standard export.

Complex inline elements support nested payloads:
- A word with an inline annotation: {DirectWrite Text Layout|Hardware-accelerated text shaping engine for OpenType features}.
- An inline footnote reference(fn: Footnotes in Ulysses and Odisea are automatically numbered on output and mapped to bottom-of-page or end-of-section slots).
- Technical inline code `const layout = engine.create_text_layout(text);` and inline raw string ~<span class="custom-win11-pill">Native</span>~.

## Lists and Task Tracking

Odisea supports nested hierarchical lists with smart indentation:

1. Phase 1: Core Parsing & Lexical Analysis
   1. Build unambiguous EBNF grammar
   2. Implement zero-copy Rust/C++ lexer
2. Phase 2: Layout & Typography Engine
   - [x] Baseline grid alignment (16pt pitch)
   - [x] Multi-column balancing (PDF & print)
   - [ ] DirectWrite typography fallback for OpenType math
3. Phase 3: High-Fidelity UI Components
   * File library navigation tree (SQLite backend)
   * Three-pane fluid layout (Library, Sheet List, Editor)

## Block Quotes and Structural Nesting

> The true beauty of a focused text editor lies in the invisible discipline of its layout engine.
> When text snaps seamlessly to the **baseline grid**(fn: Ulysses baseline grid feature aligns every line across all columns strictly), the reading experience becomes effortless.
> > Nested block quotes inherit typography while compounding margin indents and accent borders.

## Mathematical Typography (LaTeX Equations)

Odisea provides first-class LaTeX mathematical formulas both inline and as standalone display blocks:

Inline equation: The relativistic energy-momentum invariant is $E^2 = (pc)^2 + (m_0 c^2)^2$.

Standalone display equation block:

$$\oint_{\partial \Omega} \mathbf{E} \cdot d\mathbf{A} = \frac{1}{\varepsilon_0} \iiint_{\Omega} \rho \, dV$$

## Code Blocks & Verbatim Raw Blocks

Code blocks support language specifiers and tab stops:

''rust
pub struct SheetParser {
    tokens: Vec<Token>,
    cursor: usize,
}

impl SheetParser {
    pub fn parse_markdown_xl(input: &str) -> Result<DocumentNode, ParseError> {
        // High performance SIMD scanner
        let lexer = Lexer::new(input);
        lexer.tokenize_all()
    }
}
''

Verbatim raw blocks bypass the markup engine and feed directly into target exporter backends:

~~
\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=blue!5!white,colframe=blue!75!black,title=Windows 11 Integration]
DirectComposition Visual tree synchronized with Windows DWM compositor.
\end{tcolorbox}
~~

